{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAWgW7WGCERLp4eE1Lvf7E","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/config/render.go:97:\tMaxReviewRounds int      `yaml:\"max_review_rounds,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:163:\t\t\tMaxReviewRounds: role.MaxReviewRounds,\ninternal/config/testdata/resolved.golden:87:    max_review_rounds: 3\ninternal/config/types.go:126:\tMaxReviewRounds int      // default 3\ninternal/config/defaults.go:39:\tdefaultWorkerMaxReviewRounds = 3\ninternal/config/load.go:54:\tmaxTestFixes, maxRounds      *int\ninternal/config/load.go:76:\tKindWorker:   {\"tests\": true, \"max_test_fixes\": true, \"max_review_rounds\": true, \"reviewers\": true},\ninternal/config/load.go:187:\t\trole.MaxReviewRounds = defaultWorkerMaxReviewRounds\ninternal/config/load.go:241:\t\tcase \"max_open\", \"group_size\", \"max_test_fixes\", \"max_review_rounds\":\ninternal/config/load.go:258:\t\t\tcase \"max_review_rounds\":\ninternal/config/load.go:259:\t\t\t\tov.maxRounds = &v\ninternal/config/load.go:394:\tif ov.maxRounds != nil {\ninternal/config/load.go:395:\t\trole.MaxReviewRounds = *ov.maxRounds\ninternal/roles/testdata/cve/scoped_npm/osv.json:112:              \"details\": \"### Impact\\n\\nUsing Babel to compile code that was specifically crafted by an attacker can lead to arbitrary code execution during compilation, when using plugins that rely on the `path.evaluate()`or `path.evaluateTruthy()` internal Babel methods.\\n\\nKnown affected plugins are:\\n- `@babel/plugin-transform-runtime`\\n- `@babel/preset-env` when using its [`useBuiltIns`](https://babeljs.io/docs/babel-preset-env#usebuiltins) option\\n- Any \\\"polyfill provider\\\" plugin that depends on `@babel/helper-define-polyfill-provider`, such as `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs2`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-es-shims`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-regenerator`\\n\\nNo other plugins under the `@babel/` namespace are impacted, but third-party plugins might be.\\n\\n**Users that only compile trusted code are not impacted.**\\n\\n### Patches\\n\\nThe vulnerability has been fixed in `@babel/traverse@7.23.2`.\\n\\nBabel 6 does not receive security fixes anymore (see [Babel's security policy](https://github.com/babel/babel/security/policy)), hence there is no patch planned for `babel-traverse@6`.\\n\\n### Workarounds\\n\\n- Upgrade `@babel/traverse` to v7.23.2 or higher. You can do this by deleting it from your package manager's lockfile and re-installing the dependencies. `@babel/core` >=7.23.2 will automatically pull in a non-vulnerable version.\\n- If you cannot upgrade `@babel/traverse` and are using one of the affected packages mentioned above, upgrade them to their latest version to avoid triggering the vulnerable code path in affected `@babel/traverse` versions:\\n  - `@babel/plugin-transform-runtime` v7.23.2\\n  - `@babel/preset-env` v7.23.2\\n  - `@babel/helper-define-polyfill-provider` v0.4.3\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs2` v0.4.6\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3` v0.8.5\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-es-shims` v0.10.0\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-regenerator` v0.5.3\",\ninternal/roles/config.yaml:33:  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:67:  whole pull request (earlier rounds count);\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:115:   whole job, including the tests and any fix rounds, so work\ndocs/proposal.md:30:    R -->|\"ard:review:ROLE:changes (max 3 rounds)\"| W\ndocs/proposal.md:283:1. **Who acts.** The Reaper kills only a job that a goroutine in this process still drives (its pool slot is held and was not adopted at startup), and only for a deadline or a quiet heartbeat; it records the reason first, and the owner's close-out reads it. A worker keeps its job after the agent exits (tests, fix rounds), so \"exited\" alone never means abandoned. Any job nobody drives (adopted after a restart, or no slot) is closed out by the Reaper itself, and its adopted slot is released. A job whose close-out has started is resumed, never failed.\ndocs/proposal.md:299:2. **Branch** `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>` from `origin/main`. The slug is the issue title lowercased, every run of other characters turned into one `-`, at most 40 ASCII characters, `issue` when nothing is left. The title can change between rounds, so the loop looks the branch up with `git ls-remote` on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-*`: one match is reused (and fetched), none is created on the first push, and more than one (only a human can make the second) posts once and adds `ard:needs-human` without claiming. Worker role names may not contain an all-digit segment (`eng-12`), so `worker/<role>-<issue#>-` names exactly one role and issue.\ndocs/proposal.md:310:**Review feedback loops back here.** When any reviewer ends with `ard:review:<role>:changes`, the controller re-requests `ard:worker:<role>` on the issue and increments the round. The worker fixes on the same branch, and only the reviewers that asked for changes run again. The merger sends a PR back the same way when its branch conflicts with `main`. After `max_review_rounds` (default 3) the issue goes to `ard:needs-human`.\ndocs/proposal.md:353:It squash-merges with the worker's commit title and the `Ard-Job` trailer, then deletes the branch, so `.ard/<issue#>/` and its logs land on `main` with the code. If updating the branch conflicts, it re-requests the worker for a rebase round, which counts toward `max_review_rounds`.\ndocs/proposal.md:405:Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts and 3 review rounds. Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `:`, leading `-`, `..` or spaces; an abbreviated SHA is rejected, use all 40 characters); `ard config check` reports the file and key. A worker's `timeout` and `max_budget_usd` cover the whole job (every step), and `tests: \"\"` disables its test step. Per-role keys are `every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `timeout`, `agent`, `model`, `max_budget_usd`, `budget_usd_per_day`, `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `reviewers` and `when` (`paths`, or `triage` roles that ran). `plan_section` is for triage roles: the `## <heading>` of `plan.md` the role owns (one line, no leading `#`, unique across triage roles). The starter roles default to Requirements (product-manager), Design (architect), UX (designer), Docs (documentation-planner) and Implementation (engineer), and a value in `config.yaml` overrides that; a triage role with none may write only its own role file. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\ndocs/proposal.md:445:| Reviewers update the PR, then nothing | No path back to the worker, no merge step | Fix rounds with a cap, then the merger lands it |\ndocs/proposal.md:469:    P1 -->|\"Gate 2: 10 merged PRs, failures under 10%\"| P2[\"Phase 2: All roles<br/>all triage roles<br/>all four reviewers<br/>review fix rounds<br/>merger loop<br/>remaining scanners\"]\npackage closeout\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tmaxInlineRunes   = 2000\n\tmaxBulletRunes   = 300\n\tmaxReviewRunes   = 60000\n\treviewFooterRoom = 2000 // runes kept free for the closing lines\n)\n\n// Review modes: how the review reached GitHub.\nconst (\n\tReviewInline  = \"inline\"  // one PR review with inline comments\n\tReviewBody    = \"body\"    // a PR review with every finding in its body\n\tReviewComment = \"comment\" // a plain PR comment (GitHub took no review)\n\tReviewFound   = \"found\"   // an earlier post was found; nothing was posted\n)\n\n// ReviewContext is what the reviewer loop knows that the role file cannot say.\n// Added is used by Prepare only and is not persisted: the plan keeps the\n// decided placement.\ntype ReviewContext struct {\n\t// MergeBase is the commit the diff was taken against.\n\tMergeBase string\n\t// Added is, per path, the head-side line ranges the PR added.\n\tAdded map[string][]gitx.LineRange `json:\"-\"`\n\t// HeadMoved is set when the PR gained code (anything outside .ard/) after\n\t// the commit the review pinned. An approve is then not a pass: the review\n\t// is posted but no label says done, so the request stays and runs again.\n\tHeadMoved bool\n}\n\n// ReviewPlan is the PR review close-out posts for a review job that reached a\n// verdict.\ntype ReviewPlan struct {\n\tCommitSHA string // the pinned commit the agent reviewed\n\tVerdict   string // after any downgrade\n\t// Downgraded: the role file said approve but carried a blocking finding.\n\tDowngraded bool\n\tHeadMoved  bool\n\tInline     []Finding // on lines the PR added: posted as inline comments\n\tOther      []Finding // everything else: listed in the review body\n\t// NoLines: the added lines were not known (a Reaper close-out after a\n\t// restart), so every finding is in Other.\n\tNoLines bool\n\t// PRGone is set (merged, closed or branch gone) when the PR was gone at\n\t// close-out: nothing was committed and the job is stale.\n\tPRGone string `json:\",omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// reviewPlan splits the findings of a review by whether their line is one the\n// PR added.\nfunc reviewPlan(j Job, verdict string, downgraded bool, fs []Finding) *ReviewPlan {\n\trp := &ReviewPlan{CommitSHA: j.BaseSHA, Verdict: verdict, Downgraded: downgraded}\n\tif j.Review == nil {\n\t\trp.NoLines, rp.HeadMoved = true, true\n\t\trp.Other = append(rp.Other, fs...)\n\t\treturn rp\n\t}\n\trp.HeadMoved = j.Review.HeadMoved\n\tfor _, f := range fs {\n\t\tif f.Line > 0 && inRanges(f.Line, j.Review.Added[f.File]) {\n\t\t\trp.Inline = append(rp.Inline, f)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\trp.Other = append(rp.Other, f)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn rp\n}\n\nfunc inRanges(line int, rs []gitx.LineRange) bool {\n\tfor _, r := range rs {\n\t\tif line >= r.From && line <= r.To {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc findingTag(f Finding) string {\n\tb := \"non-blocking\"\n\tif f.Blocking {\n\t\tb = \"blocking\"\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"**%s · %s**\", f.Severity, b)\n}\n\n// inlineBody is the text of one inline comment.\nfunc inlineBody(f Finding) string {\n\treturn findingTag(f) + \"\\n\\n\" + sanitize(cutRunes(f.Message, maxInlineRunes))\n}\n\nfunc cutRunes(s string, n int) string {\n\tif r := []rune(s); len(r) > n {\n\t\treturn string(r[:n-1]) + \"…\"\n\t}\n\treturn s\n}\n\nfunc bullet(f Finding) string {\n\tloc := f.File\n\tif f.Line > 0 {\n\t\tloc = fmt.Sprintf(\"%s:%d\", f.File, f.Line)\n\t}\n\tfirst := strings.TrimSpace(strings.SplitN(strings.TrimSpace(f.Message), \"\\n\", 2)[0])\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"- %s %s %s\", findingTag(f), codeSpan(loc, 340), sanitize(cutRunes(first, maxBulletRunes)))\n}\n\n// inlineComments builds the inline comments of a review plan.\nfunc inlineComments(rp *ReviewPlan) []github.InlineComment {\n\tout := make([]github.InlineComment, 0, len(rp.Inline))\n\tfor _, f := range rp.Inline {\n\t\tout = append(out, github.InlineComment{Path: f.File, Line: f.Line, Side: \"RIGHT\", Body: inlineBody(f)})\n\t}\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// RenderReview builds the body of the PR review (or of the plain comment that\n// replaces it). With allInBody every finding is listed in the body, for the\n// fallbacks that carry no inline comments. The body is at most 60,000 runes.\nfunc RenderReview(r Record, repo github.Repo, dryRun, allInBody bool) string {\n\tj, p := r.Job, r.Plan\n\trp := p.Review\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tb.WriteString(marker(j.ID, j.Attempt) + \"\\n\")\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"**ard · review:%s · %s**\\n\", j.Role, rp.Verdict)\n\tif s := strings.TrimSpace(p.Summary); s != \"\" {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + sanitize(cutSummary(s)) + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tvar notes []string\n\tif rp.Downgraded {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The review approved but listed a blocking finding, so ard treats it as changes requested.\")\n\t}\n\tif rp.HeadMoved && rp.PRGone == \"\" {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The branch gained code after this commit was reviewed. The review stays requested and runs again on the new head.\")\n\t}\n\tif rp.PRGone != \"\" {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The pull request was merged or closed before this review finished, so nothing was committed and the job is recorded as stale.\")\n\t}\n\tif len(notes) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + strings.Join(notes, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tlist, heading := rp.Other, \"Findings outside the changed lines:\"\n\tswitch {\n\tcase allInBody:\n\t\tlist = append(append([]Finding(nil), rp.Inline...), rp.Other...)\n\t\theading = \"Findings:\"\n\tcase rp.NoLines:\n\t\theading = \"Findings (line placement unavailable):\"\n\t}\n\tif len(list) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + heading + \"\\n\")\n\t\tused := len([]rune(b.String()))\n\t\tfor i, f := range list {\n\t\t\tline := bullet(f)\n\t\t\tif used+len([]rune(line))+1 > maxReviewRunes-reviewFooterRoom {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"- … and %d more in the committed file\\n\", len(list)-i)\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tb.WriteString(line + \"\\n\")\n\t\t\tused += len([]rune(line)) + 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar lines []string\n\tif sha := rp.CommitSHA; sha != \"\" {\n\t\tif len(sha) > 12 {\n\t\t\tsha = sha[:12]\n\t\t}\n\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"Reviewed commit `%s`\", sha))\n\t}\n\tif out := outputLine(r, repo, dryRun); out != \"\" {\n\t\tlines = append(lines, out)\n\t}\n\tif len(lines) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn b.String()\n}\npackage reviewer\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agentjob\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/closeout\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/intake\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/modelauth\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/pool\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/reaper\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tdefaultInterval = 5 * time.Minute\n\tdefaultPoll     = 2 * time.Second\n\tstageReview     = \"review\"\n)\n\n// Reader is the part of github.Reader the loop uses.\ntype Reader interface {\n\tIdentity(ctx context.Context) (github.Identity, error)\n\tGetIssue(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.Issue, error)\n\tGetPR(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.PullRequest, error)\n\tSearchIssues(ctx context.Context, q string, o github.SearchOpts) ([]github.Issue, error)\n\tListComments(ctx context.Context, n int, since time.Time) ([]github.Comment, error)\n}\n\n// Effects is the part of effects.Effects the loop uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tAddLabels(ctx context.Context, n int, labels ...string) error\n\tRemoveLabel(ctx context.Context, n int, label string) error\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tMarkReady(ctx context.Context, n int) error\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Store is the part of *state.Store the loop uses.\ntype Store interface {\n\tCreateJob(ctx context.Context, n state.NewJob) (state.Job, error)\n\tSetHandle(ctx context.Context, id string, h json.RawMessage) error\n\tStartAttempt(ctx context.Context, id string) (int, error)\n\tFail(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tRunningJobs(ctx context.Context) ([]state.Job, error)\n\tAdmission(ctx context.Context, issue int) (state.Admission, error)\n\tSetAdmission(ctx context.Context, a state.Admission) error\n\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n}\n\n// Finisher is *reaper.Finisher: the one way a started job ends.\ntype Finisher interface {\n\tFinishWith(ctx context.Context, jobID string, h executor.Handle, st executor.Status, res agent.Result, o reaper.FinishOptions) (closeout.Outcome, error)\n}\n\n// Git is the read side of *gitx.Git, run against the controller's clone only.\n// It has no Commit or Push: only internal/effects may call those.\ntype Git interface {\n\tFetchRef(ctx context.Context, repoDir, url, refspec string, token gitx.TokenFunc) error\n\tRevParse(ctx context.Context, dir, ref string) (string, error)\n\tMergeBase(ctx context.Context, repoDir, a, b string) (string, error)\n\tDiff(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, maxBytes int64, exclude ...string) ([]byte, bool, error)\n\tAddedLinesBetween(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, exclude ...string) (map[string][]gitx.LineRange, error)\n\tCodeChanged(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, exclude ...string) ([]string, error)\n}\n\n// Offerer is *pool.Pool.\ntype Offerer interface {\n\tOffer(loop string, ttl time.Duration, cands []pool.Candidate) []pool.Decision\n}\n\n// Deps are the loop's collaborators. Executor, Finisher and Parse must be the\n// ones the Reaper uses: the Reaper asks the same executor, and the Finisher\n// shares the one Closer.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tReader   Reader\n\tEffects  Effects\n\tStore    Store\n\tExecutor executor.Executor\n\tFinisher Finisher\n\tGit      Git\n\tPool     func() Offerer // called at tick time: the pool does not exist when loops are built\n\tAgents   *agent.Registry\n\tParse    reaper.ParseFunc\n\tModel    modelauth.Credential // zero = none set\n\n\tRepo      github.Repo\n\tRepoDir   string // absolute path of the controller's clone\n\tRemoteURL string\n\tToken     gitx.TokenFunc\n\tPoll      time.Duration // Status poll interval; default 2s\n\tNow       func() time.Time\n\tLog       *slog.Logger\n}\n\n// Loop is the reviewer loop. It implements controller.Loop.\ntype Loop struct {\n\td Deps\n\n\tmu     sync.Mutex\n\tnoCred bool\n}\n\nvar _ controller.Loop = (*Loop)(nil)\n\n// New returns the loop with defaults applied.\nfunc New(d Deps) *Loop {\n\tif d.Poll <= 0 {\n\t\td.Poll = defaultPoll\n\t}\n\tif d.Now == nil {\n\t\td.Now = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif d.Log == nil {\n\t\td.Log = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Loop{d: d}\n}\n\n// Name implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Name() string { return \"reviewers\" }\n\n// Interval implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Interval(c *config.Resolved) time.Duration {\n\tif c == nil || c.Intervals.Reviewers <= 0 {\n\t\treturn defaultInterval\n\t}\n\treturn time.Duration(c.Intervals.Reviewers)\n}\n\n// TickTimeout implements controller.TickTimeouter. A tick never waits for a\n// job.\nfunc (*Loop) TickTimeout(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return 5 * time.Minute }\n\n// Claims implements controller.Loop: the loop is skipped while paused.\nfunc (*Loop) Claims() bool { return true }\n\nfunc (l *Loop) offer(cfg *config.Resolved, cands []pool.Candidate) []pool.Decision {\n\treturn l.d.Pool().Offer(l.Name(), 2*l.Interval(cfg), cands)\n}\n\n// Tick implements controller.Loop. Errors for one PR are logged and joined, so\n// one bad PR never stops the others.\nfunc (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, env controller.Env) error {\n\tcfg := env.Cfg\n\tlog := env.Log\n\tif log == nil {\n\t\tlog = l.d.Log\n\t}\n\tif cfg == nil || cfg.SHA == \"\" || len(cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer)) == 0 {\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdry := l.d.Effects.DryRun()\n\tid, err := l.d.Reader.Identity(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"review: identify github user: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tt := &tick{l: l, cfg: cfg, log: log, self: id.Login, dry: dry}\n\t// The sweep needs no agent, so it runs before the credential check.\n\tt.sweepReady(ctx)\n\tif _, err := l.d.Model.Require(); err != nil && !dry {\n\t\tl.mu.Lock()\n\t\tfirst := !l.noCred\n\t\tl.noCred = true\n\t\tl.mu.Unlock()\n\t\tif first {\n\t\t\tlog.Warn(\"review.no_model_credential\", \"hint\", \"agent jobs will not be claimed until one is set\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tcands, errs := t.candidates(ctx)\n\n\tif dry {\n\t\tfor _, c := range cands {\n\t\t\tlog.Info(\"review.would_claim\", \"pr\", c.pr.Number, \"issue\", c.issue.Number, \"role\", c.role.Name)\n\t\t}\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn errors.Join(errs...)\n\t}\n\n\tpcs := make([]pool.Candidate, len(cands))\n\tfor i, c := range cands {\n\t\tpcs[i] = pool.Candidate{Class: pool.ClassReview, Role: c.role.Name, Number: c.pr.Number, Since: c.since}\n\t}\n\tdecs := l.offer(cfg, pcs)\n\tstopped := false\n\tfor i, d := range decs {\n\t\tif d.Verdict != pool.Granted || d.Slot == nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif stopped {\n\t\t\td.Slot.Release()\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tc := cands[i]\n\t\tname := fmt.Sprintf(\"review:%s:%d\", c.role.Name, c.pr.Number)\n\t\tslot := d.Slot\n\t\tif err := env.Inflight.Go(name, func(wctx context.Context) { l.run(wctx, env, cfg, c, slot) }); err != nil {\n\t\t\tslot.Release()\n\t\t\tstopped = true\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review: %w\", err))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn errors.Join(errs...)\n}\n\n// tick holds what one Tick passes between its steps.\ntype tick struct {\n\tl    *Loop\n\tcfg  *config.Resolved\n\tlog  *slog.Logger\n\tself string\n\tdry  bool\n}\n\n// recheck is the admission re-check a human-filed issue goes through.\nfunc (t *tick) recheck() agentjob.Recheck {\n\td := t.l.d\n\treturn agentjob.Recheck{Stage: \"review\", Stopped: \"reviewing\", Label: intake.Label(t.cfg.Intake),\n\t\tSelf: t.self, Dry: t.dry, Log: t.log, Store: d.Store, Reader: d.Reader, Effects: d.Effects}\n}\npackage reviewer\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github/query\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n)\n\n// candidate is a PR a reviewer role may claim, with the fresh re-read of the\n// PR and its issue.\ntype candidate struct {\n\trole  config.Role\n\tpr    github.PullRequest\n\tissue github.Issue\n\tsince time.Time\n}\n\n// Skip reasons, fixed text for the review.skip log line.\nconst (\n\tskipNotAppPR      = \"not_app_pr\"\n\tskipNotWorkerRef  = \"not_worker_branch\"\n\tskipBaseNotMain   = \"base_not_main\"\n\tskipIssueClosed   = \"issue_closed\"\n\tskipIssueBlocked  = \"issue_blocked\"\n\tskipWorkerRunning = \"worker_running\"\n)\n\n// excludedLabels are the labels that keep a PR out of a reviewer role's\n// queries: its own states and the guards.\nfunc excludedLabels(role string) []string {\n\treturn []string{\n\t\tlabels.Running(labels.StageReview, role), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, role), labels.Changes(role),\n\t\tlabels.ExecutorFailed, labels.NeedsHuman, labels.Hold, labels.TestsFailed,\n\t}\n}\n\n// candidates finds, per reviewer role, the PRs that request it and pass every\n// check. A review job of another role on the same PR does not exclude it:\n// reviewers run in parallel and their commits serialise on the branch lane.\nfunc (t *tick) candidates(ctx context.Context) ([]candidate, []error) {\n\tl := t.l\n\trunning, err := l.d.Store.RunningJobs(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, []error{fmt.Errorf(\"review: list running jobs: %w\", err)}\n\t}\n\tworkerBusy := map[int]bool{}\n\tfor _, j := range running {\n\t\tif j.Stage == \"worker\" {\n\t\t\tworkerBusy[j.Issue] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar out []candidate\n\tvar errs []error\n\tfor _, role := range t.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer) {\n\t\tq, err := query.RoleQuery{\n\t\t\tType: query.TypePR, Request: labels.Request(labels.StageReview, role.Name),\n\t\t\tStates: []string{labels.Running(labels.StageReview, role.Name), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, role.Name), labels.Changes(role.Name)},\n\t\t\tGuards: []string{labels.ExecutorFailed, labels.NeedsHuman, labels.Hold, labels.TestsFailed},\n\t\t}.Build()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review role %s: %w\", role.Name, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\thits, err := l.d.Reader.SearchIssues(ctx, q, github.SearchOpts{Sort: \"created\", Order: \"asc\", Max: 50})\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review role %s: search: %w\", role.Name, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, hit := range hits {\n\t\t\tc, ok, err := t.consider(ctx, role, hit, workerBusy)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\terrs = append(errs, err)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif ok {\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, c)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, errs\n}\n\nfunc (t *tick) skip(pr int, role, reason string) {\n\tt.log.Info(\"review.skip\", \"pr\", pr, \"role\", role, \"reason\", reason)\n}\n\n// consider re-reads PR hit.Number (search is eventually consistent) and its\n// issue, then applies the rules in the package comment.\nfunc (t *tick) consider(ctx context.Context, role config.Role, hit github.Issue, workerBusy map[int]bool) (candidate, bool, error) {\n\tl := t.l\n\tn := hit.Number\n\tpr, err := l.d.Reader.GetPR(ctx, n)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) {\n\t\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"review PR %d: re-read: %w\", n, err)\n\t}\n\tif pr.State != github.StateOpen || pr.Merged || !hasLabel(pr.Labels, labels.Request(labels.StageReview, role.Name)) ||\n\t\thasAny(pr.Labels, excludedLabels(role.Name)) {\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tif !strings.EqualFold(pr.Author, t.self) {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipNotAppPR)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tif pr.BaseRef != \"main\" {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipBaseNotMain)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\t_, issueN, ok := parseWorkerBranch(pr.HeadRef)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipNotWorkerRef)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tis, err := l.d.Reader.GetIssue(ctx, issueN)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) {\n\t\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueClosed)\n\t\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"review PR %d: read issue %d: %w\", n, issueN, err)\n\t}\n\tswitch {\n\tcase is.State != github.StateOpen || is.IsPR:\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueClosed)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\tcase hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.NeedsHuman) || hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.Hold):\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueBlocked)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\tcase workerBusy[issueN]:\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipWorkerRunning)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tok, err = t.recheck().Admitted(ctx, is)\n\tif err != nil || !ok {\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, err\n\t}\n\treturn candidate{role: role, pr: pr, issue: is, since: hit.CreatedAt}, true, nil\n}\n\nfunc hasAny(have []string, want []string) bool {\n\tfor _, w := range want {\n\t\tif hasLabel(have, w) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc hasLabel(have []string, want string) bool {\n\tfor _, h := range have {\n\t\tif strings.EqualFold(h, want) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91239cb8-ffdf-4c30-aff0-585345086adf","uuid":"db08222f-7132-4a76-bf89-42c5cec6cb82","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:06:01.870Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"internal/config/render.go:97:\tMaxReviewRounds int      `yaml:\"max_review_rounds,omitempty\"`\ninternal/config/render.go:163:\t\t\tMaxReviewRounds: role.MaxReviewRounds,\ninternal/config/testdata/resolved.golden:87:    max_review_rounds: 3\ninternal/config/types.go:126:\tMaxReviewRounds int      // default 3\ninternal/config/defaults.go:39:\tdefaultWorkerMaxReviewRounds = 3\ninternal/config/load.go:54:\tmaxTestFixes, maxRounds      *int\ninternal/config/load.go:76:\tKindWorker:   {\"tests\": true, \"max_test_fixes\": true, \"max_review_rounds\": true, \"reviewers\": true},\ninternal/config/load.go:187:\t\trole.MaxReviewRounds = defaultWorkerMaxReviewRounds\ninternal/config/load.go:241:\t\tcase \"max_open\", \"group_size\", \"max_test_fixes\", \"max_review_rounds\":\ninternal/config/load.go:258:\t\t\tcase \"max_review_rounds\":\ninternal/config/load.go:259:\t\t\t\tov.maxRounds = &v\ninternal/config/load.go:394:\tif ov.maxRounds != nil {\ninternal/config/load.go:395:\t\trole.MaxReviewRounds = *ov.maxRounds\ninternal/roles/testdata/cve/scoped_npm/osv.json:112:              \"details\": \"### Impact\\n\\nUsing Babel to compile code that was specifically crafted by an attacker can lead to arbitrary code execution during compilation, when using plugins that rely on the `path.evaluate()`or `path.evaluateTruthy()` internal Babel methods.\\n\\nKnown affected plugins are:\\n- `@babel/plugin-transform-runtime`\\n- `@babel/preset-env` when using its [`useBuiltIns`](https://babeljs.io/docs/babel-preset-env#usebuiltins) option\\n- Any \\\"polyfill provider\\\" plugin that depends on `@babel/helper-define-polyfill-provider`, such as `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs2`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-es-shims`, `babel-plugin-polyfill-regenerator`\\n\\nNo other plugins under the `@babel/` namespace are impacted, but third-party plugins might be.\\n\\n**Users that only compile trusted code are not impacted.**\\n\\n### Patches\\n\\nThe vulnerability has been fixed in `@babel/traverse@7.23.2`.\\n\\nBabel 6 does not receive security fixes anymore (see [Babel's security policy](https://github.com/babel/babel/security/policy)), hence there is no patch planned for `babel-traverse@6`.\\n\\n### Workarounds\\n\\n- Upgrade `@babel/traverse` to v7.23.2 or higher. You can do this by deleting it from your package manager's lockfile and re-installing the dependencies. `@babel/core` >=7.23.2 will automatically pull in a non-vulnerable version.\\n- If you cannot upgrade `@babel/traverse` and are using one of the affected packages mentioned above, upgrade them to their latest version to avoid triggering the vulnerable code path in affected `@babel/traverse` versions:\\n  - `@babel/plugin-transform-runtime` v7.23.2\\n  - `@babel/preset-env` v7.23.2\\n  - `@babel/helper-define-polyfill-provider` v0.4.3\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs2` v0.4.6\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-corejs3` v0.8.5\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-es-shims` v0.10.0\\n  - `babel-plugin-polyfill-regenerator` v0.5.3\",\ninternal/roles/config.yaml:33:  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:67:  whole pull request (earlier rounds count);\ninternal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt:115:   whole job, including the tests and any fix rounds, so work\ndocs/proposal.md:30:    R -->|\"ard:review:ROLE:changes (max 3 rounds)\"| W\ndocs/proposal.md:283:1. **Who acts.** The Reaper kills only a job that a goroutine in this process still drives (its pool slot is held and was not adopted at startup), and only for a deadline or a quiet heartbeat; it records the reason first, and the owner's close-out reads it. A worker keeps its job after the agent exits (tests, fix rounds), so \"exited\" alone never means abandoned. Any job nobody drives (adopted after a restart, or no slot) is closed out by the Reaper itself, and its adopted slot is released. A job whose close-out has started is resumed, never failed.\ndocs/proposal.md:299:2. **Branch** `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>` from `origin/main`. The slug is the issue title lowercased, every run of other characters turned into one `-`, at most 40 ASCII characters, `issue` when nothing is left. The title can change between rounds, so the loop looks the branch up with `git ls-remote` on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-*`: one match is reused (and fetched), none is created on the first push, and more than one (only a human can make the second) posts once and adds `ard:needs-human` without claiming. Worker role names may not contain an all-digit segment (`eng-12`), so `worker/<role>-<issue#>-` names exactly one role and issue.\ndocs/proposal.md:310:**Review feedback loops back here.** When any reviewer ends with `ard:review:<role>:changes`, the controller re-requests `ard:worker:<role>` on the issue and increments the round. The worker fixes on the same branch, and only the reviewers that asked for changes run again. The merger sends a PR back the same way when its branch conflicts with `main`. After `max_review_rounds` (default 3) the issue goes to `ard:needs-human`.\ndocs/proposal.md:353:It squash-merges with the worker's commit title and the `Ard-Job` trailer, then deletes the branch, so `.ard/<issue#>/` and its logs land on `main` with the code. If updating the branch conflicts, it re-requests the worker for a rebase round, which counts toward `max_review_rounds`.\ndocs/proposal.md:405:Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts and 3 review rounds. Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `:`, leading `-`, `..` or spaces; an abbreviated SHA is rejected, use all 40 characters); `ard config check` reports the file and key. A worker's `timeout` and `max_budget_usd` cover the whole job (every step), and `tests: \"\"` disables its test step. Per-role keys are `every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `timeout`, `agent`, `model`, `max_budget_usd`, `budget_usd_per_day`, `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `reviewers` and `when` (`paths`, or `triage` roles that ran). `plan_section` is for triage roles: the `## <heading>` of `plan.md` the role owns (one line, no leading `#`, unique across triage roles). The starter roles default to Requirements (product-manager), Design (architect), UX (designer), Docs (documentation-planner) and Implementation (engineer), and a value in `config.yaml` overrides that; a triage role with none may write only its own role file. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\ndocs/proposal.md:445:| Reviewers update the PR, then nothing | No path back to the worker, no merge step | Fix rounds with a cap, then the merger lands it |\ndocs/proposal.md:469:    P1 -->|\"Gate 2: 10 merged PRs, failures under 10%\"| P2[\"Phase 2: All roles<br/>all triage roles<br/>all four reviewers<br/>review fix rounds<br/>merger loop<br/>remaining scanners\"]\npackage closeout\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tmaxInlineRunes   = 2000\n\tmaxBulletRunes   = 300\n\tmaxReviewRunes   = 60000\n\treviewFooterRoom = 2000 // runes kept free for the closing lines\n)\n\n// Review modes: how the review reached GitHub.\nconst (\n\tReviewInline  = \"inline\"  // one PR review with inline comments\n\tReviewBody    = \"body\"    // a PR review with every finding in its body\n\tReviewComment = \"comment\" // a plain PR comment (GitHub took no review)\n\tReviewFound   = \"found\"   // an earlier post was found; nothing was posted\n)\n\n// ReviewContext is what the reviewer loop knows that the role file cannot say.\n// Added is used by Prepare only and is not persisted: the plan keeps the\n// decided placement.\ntype ReviewContext struct {\n\t// MergeBase is the commit the diff was taken against.\n\tMergeBase string\n\t// Added is, per path, the head-side line ranges the PR added.\n\tAdded map[string][]gitx.LineRange `json:\"-\"`\n\t// HeadMoved is set when the PR gained code (anything outside .ard/) after\n\t// the commit the review pinned. An approve is then not a pass: the review\n\t// is posted but no label says done, so the request stays and runs again.\n\tHeadMoved bool\n}\n\n// ReviewPlan is the PR review close-out posts for a review job that reached a\n// verdict.\ntype ReviewPlan struct {\n\tCommitSHA string // the pinned commit the agent reviewed\n\tVerdict   string // after any downgrade\n\t// Downgraded: the role file said approve but carried a blocking finding.\n\tDowngraded bool\n\tHeadMoved  bool\n\tInline     []Finding // on lines the PR added: posted as inline comments\n\tOther      []Finding // everything else: listed in the review body\n\t// NoLines: the added lines were not known (a Reaper close-out after a\n\t// restart), so every finding is in Other.\n\tNoLines bool\n\t// PRGone is set (merged, closed or branch gone) when the PR was gone at\n\t// close-out: nothing was committed and the job is stale.\n\tPRGone string `json:\",omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// reviewPlan splits the findings of a review by whether their line is one the\n// PR added.\nfunc reviewPlan(j Job, verdict string, downgraded bool, fs []Finding) *ReviewPlan {\n\trp := &ReviewPlan{CommitSHA: j.BaseSHA, Verdict: verdict, Downgraded: downgraded}\n\tif j.Review == nil {\n\t\trp.NoLines, rp.HeadMoved = true, true\n\t\trp.Other = append(rp.Other, fs...)\n\t\treturn rp\n\t}\n\trp.HeadMoved = j.Review.HeadMoved\n\tfor _, f := range fs {\n\t\tif f.Line > 0 && inRanges(f.Line, j.Review.Added[f.File]) {\n\t\t\trp.Inline = append(rp.Inline, f)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\trp.Other = append(rp.Other, f)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn rp\n}\n\nfunc inRanges(line int, rs []gitx.LineRange) bool {\n\tfor _, r := range rs {\n\t\tif line >= r.From && line <= r.To {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc findingTag(f Finding) string {\n\tb := \"non-blocking\"\n\tif f.Blocking {\n\t\tb = \"blocking\"\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"**%s · %s**\", f.Severity, b)\n}\n\n// inlineBody is the text of one inline comment.\nfunc inlineBody(f Finding) string {\n\treturn findingTag(f) + \"\\n\\n\" + sanitize(cutRunes(f.Message, maxInlineRunes))\n}\n\nfunc cutRunes(s string, n int) string {\n\tif r := []rune(s); len(r) > n {\n\t\treturn string(r[:n-1]) + \"…\"\n\t}\n\treturn s\n}\n\nfunc bullet(f Finding) string {\n\tloc := f.File\n\tif f.Line > 0 {\n\t\tloc = fmt.Sprintf(\"%s:%d\", f.File, f.Line)\n\t}\n\tfirst := strings.TrimSpace(strings.SplitN(strings.TrimSpace(f.Message), \"\\n\", 2)[0])\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"- %s %s %s\", findingTag(f), codeSpan(loc, 340), sanitize(cutRunes(first, maxBulletRunes)))\n}\n\n// inlineComments builds the inline comments of a review plan.\nfunc inlineComments(rp *ReviewPlan) []github.InlineComment {\n\tout := make([]github.InlineComment, 0, len(rp.Inline))\n\tfor _, f := range rp.Inline {\n\t\tout = append(out, github.InlineComment{Path: f.File, Line: f.Line, Side: \"RIGHT\", Body: inlineBody(f)})\n\t}\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// RenderReview builds the body of the PR review (or of the plain comment that\n// replaces it). With allInBody every finding is listed in the body, for the\n// fallbacks that carry no inline comments. The body is at most 60,000 runes.\nfunc RenderReview(r Record, repo github.Repo, dryRun, allInBody bool) string {\n\tj, p := r.Job, r.Plan\n\trp := p.Review\n\tvar b strings.Builder\n\tb.WriteString(marker(j.ID, j.Attempt) + \"\\n\")\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"**ard · review:%s · %s**\\n\", j.Role, rp.Verdict)\n\tif s := strings.TrimSpace(p.Summary); s != \"\" {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + sanitize(cutSummary(s)) + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tvar notes []string\n\tif rp.Downgraded {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The review approved but listed a blocking finding, so ard treats it as changes requested.\")\n\t}\n\tif rp.HeadMoved && rp.PRGone == \"\" {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The branch gained code after this commit was reviewed. The review stays requested and runs again on the new head.\")\n\t}\n\tif rp.PRGone != \"\" {\n\t\tnotes = append(notes, \"The pull request was merged or closed before this review finished, so nothing was committed and the job is recorded as stale.\")\n\t}\n\tif len(notes) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + strings.Join(notes, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tlist, heading := rp.Other, \"Findings outside the changed lines:\"\n\tswitch {\n\tcase allInBody:\n\t\tlist = append(append([]Finding(nil), rp.Inline...), rp.Other...)\n\t\theading = \"Findings:\"\n\tcase rp.NoLines:\n\t\theading = \"Findings (line placement unavailable):\"\n\t}\n\tif len(list) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + heading + \"\\n\")\n\t\tused := len([]rune(b.String()))\n\t\tfor i, f := range list {\n\t\t\tline := bullet(f)\n\t\t\tif used+len([]rune(line))+1 > maxReviewRunes-reviewFooterRoom {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"- … and %d more in the committed file\\n\", len(list)-i)\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tb.WriteString(line + \"\\n\")\n\t\t\tused += len([]rune(line)) + 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar lines []string\n\tif sha := rp.CommitSHA; sha != \"\" {\n\t\tif len(sha) > 12 {\n\t\t\tsha = sha[:12]\n\t\t}\n\t\tlines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf(\"Reviewed commit `%s`\", sha))\n\t}\n\tif out := outputLine(r, repo, dryRun); out != \"\" {\n\t\tlines = append(lines, out)\n\t}\n\tif len(lines) > 0 {\n\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\" + strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn b.String()\n}\npackage reviewer\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agentjob\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/closeout\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/intake\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/modelauth\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/pool\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/reaper\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tdefaultInterval = 5 * time.Minute\n\tdefaultPoll     = 2 * time.Second\n\tstageReview     = \"review\"\n)\n\n// Reader is the part of github.Reader the loop uses.\ntype Reader interface {\n\tIdentity(ctx context.Context) (github.Identity, error)\n\tGetIssue(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.Issue, error)\n\tGetPR(ctx context.Context, n int) (github.PullRequest, error)\n\tSearchIssues(ctx context.Context, q string, o github.SearchOpts) ([]github.Issue, error)\n\tListComments(ctx context.Context, n int, since time.Time) ([]github.Comment, error)\n}\n\n// Effects is the part of effects.Effects the loop uses.\ntype Effects interface {\n\tAddLabels(ctx context.Context, n int, labels ...string) error\n\tRemoveLabel(ctx context.Context, n int, label string) error\n\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n\tMarkReady(ctx context.Context, n int) error\n\tDryRun() bool\n}\n\n// Store is the part of *state.Store the loop uses.\ntype Store interface {\n\tCreateJob(ctx context.Context, n state.NewJob) (state.Job, error)\n\tSetHandle(ctx context.Context, id string, h json.RawMessage) error\n\tStartAttempt(ctx context.Context, id string) (int, error)\n\tFail(ctx context.Context, id, reason string, keepUntil time.Time) error\n\tRunningJobs(ctx context.Context) ([]state.Job, error)\n\tAdmission(ctx context.Context, issue int) (state.Admission, error)\n\tSetAdmission(ctx context.Context, a state.Admission) error\n\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n}\n\n// Finisher is *reaper.Finisher: the one way a started job ends.\ntype Finisher interface {\n\tFinishWith(ctx context.Context, jobID string, h executor.Handle, st executor.Status, res agent.Result, o reaper.FinishOptions) (closeout.Outcome, error)\n}\n\n// Git is the read side of *gitx.Git, run against the controller's clone only.\n// It has no Commit or Push: only internal/effects may call those.\ntype Git interface {\n\tFetchRef(ctx context.Context, repoDir, url, refspec string, token gitx.TokenFunc) error\n\tRevParse(ctx context.Context, dir, ref string) (string, error)\n\tMergeBase(ctx context.Context, repoDir, a, b string) (string, error)\n\tDiff(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, maxBytes int64, exclude ...string) ([]byte, bool, error)\n\tAddedLinesBetween(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, exclude ...string) (map[string][]gitx.LineRange, error)\n\tCodeChanged(ctx context.Context, repoDir, from, to string, exclude ...string) ([]string, error)\n}\n\n// Offerer is *pool.Pool.\ntype Offerer interface {\n\tOffer(loop string, ttl time.Duration, cands []pool.Candidate) []pool.Decision\n}\n\n// Deps are the loop's collaborators. Executor, Finisher and Parse must be the\n// ones the Reaper uses: the Reaper asks the same executor, and the Finisher\n// shares the one Closer.\ntype Deps struct {\n\tReader   Reader\n\tEffects  Effects\n\tStore    Store\n\tExecutor executor.Executor\n\tFinisher Finisher\n\tGit      Git\n\tPool     func() Offerer // called at tick time: the pool does not exist when loops are built\n\tAgents   *agent.Registry\n\tParse    reaper.ParseFunc\n\tModel    modelauth.Credential // zero = none set\n\n\tRepo      github.Repo\n\tRepoDir   string // absolute path of the controller's clone\n\tRemoteURL string\n\tToken     gitx.TokenFunc\n\tPoll      time.Duration // Status poll interval; default 2s\n\tNow       func() time.Time\n\tLog       *slog.Logger\n}\n\n// Loop is the reviewer loop. It implements controller.Loop.\ntype Loop struct {\n\td Deps\n\n\tmu     sync.Mutex\n\tnoCred bool\n}\n\nvar _ controller.Loop = (*Loop)(nil)\n\n// New returns the loop with defaults applied.\nfunc New(d Deps) *Loop {\n\tif d.Poll <= 0 {\n\t\td.Poll = defaultPoll\n\t}\n\tif d.Now == nil {\n\t\td.Now = time.Now\n\t}\n\tif d.Log == nil {\n\t\td.Log = slog.Default()\n\t}\n\treturn &Loop{d: d}\n}\n\n// Name implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Name() string { return \"reviewers\" }\n\n// Interval implements controller.Loop.\nfunc (*Loop) Interval(c *config.Resolved) time.Duration {\n\tif c == nil || c.Intervals.Reviewers <= 0 {\n\t\treturn defaultInterval\n\t}\n\treturn time.Duration(c.Intervals.Reviewers)\n}\n\n// TickTimeout implements controller.TickTimeouter. A tick never waits for a\n// job.\nfunc (*Loop) TickTimeout(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return 5 * time.Minute }\n\n// Claims implements controller.Loop: the loop is skipped while paused.\nfunc (*Loop) Claims() bool { return true }\n\nfunc (l *Loop) offer(cfg *config.Resolved, cands []pool.Candidate) []pool.Decision {\n\treturn l.d.Pool().Offer(l.Name(), 2*l.Interval(cfg), cands)\n}\n\n// Tick implements controller.Loop. Errors for one PR are logged and joined, so\n// one bad PR never stops the others.\nfunc (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, env controller.Env) error {\n\tcfg := env.Cfg\n\tlog := env.Log\n\tif log == nil {\n\t\tlog = l.d.Log\n\t}\n\tif cfg == nil || cfg.SHA == \"\" || len(cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer)) == 0 {\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdry := l.d.Effects.DryRun()\n\tid, err := l.d.Reader.Identity(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"review: identify github user: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tt := &tick{l: l, cfg: cfg, log: log, self: id.Login, dry: dry}\n\t// The sweep needs no agent, so it runs before the credential check.\n\tt.sweepReady(ctx)\n\tif _, err := l.d.Model.Require(); err != nil && !dry {\n\t\tl.mu.Lock()\n\t\tfirst := !l.noCred\n\t\tl.noCred = true\n\t\tl.mu.Unlock()\n\t\tif first {\n\t\t\tlog.Warn(\"review.no_model_credential\", \"hint\", \"agent jobs will not be claimed until one is set\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tcands, errs := t.candidates(ctx)\n\n\tif dry {\n\t\tfor _, c := range cands {\n\t\t\tlog.Info(\"review.would_claim\", \"pr\", c.pr.Number, \"issue\", c.issue.Number, \"role\", c.role.Name)\n\t\t}\n\t\tl.offer(cfg, nil)\n\t\treturn errors.Join(errs...)\n\t}\n\n\tpcs := make([]pool.Candidate, len(cands))\n\tfor i, c := range cands {\n\t\tpcs[i] = pool.Candidate{Class: pool.ClassReview, Role: c.role.Name, Number: c.pr.Number, Since: c.since}\n\t}\n\tdecs := l.offer(cfg, pcs)\n\tstopped := false\n\tfor i, d := range decs {\n\t\tif d.Verdict != pool.Granted || d.Slot == nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif stopped {\n\t\t\td.Slot.Release()\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tc := cands[i]\n\t\tname := fmt.Sprintf(\"review:%s:%d\", c.role.Name, c.pr.Number)\n\t\tslot := d.Slot\n\t\tif err := env.Inflight.Go(name, func(wctx context.Context) { l.run(wctx, env, cfg, c, slot) }); err != nil {\n\t\t\tslot.Release()\n\t\t\tstopped = true\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review: %w\", err))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn errors.Join(errs...)\n}\n\n// tick holds what one Tick passes between its steps.\ntype tick struct {\n\tl    *Loop\n\tcfg  *config.Resolved\n\tlog  *slog.Logger\n\tself string\n\tdry  bool\n}\n\n// recheck is the admission re-check a human-filed issue goes through.\nfunc (t *tick) recheck() agentjob.Recheck {\n\td := t.l.d\n\treturn agentjob.Recheck{Stage: \"review\", Stopped: \"reviewing\", Label: intake.Label(t.cfg.Intake),\n\t\tSelf: t.self, Dry: t.dry, Log: t.log, Store: d.Store, Reader: d.Reader, Effects: d.Effects}\n}\npackage reviewer\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github/query\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n)\n\n// candidate is a PR a reviewer role may claim, with the fresh re-read of the\n// PR and its issue.\ntype candidate struct {\n\trole  config.Role\n\tpr    github.PullRequest\n\tissue github.Issue\n\tsince time.Time\n}\n\n// Skip reasons, fixed text for the review.skip log line.\nconst (\n\tskipNotAppPR      = \"not_app_pr\"\n\tskipNotWorkerRef  = \"not_worker_branch\"\n\tskipBaseNotMain   = \"base_not_main\"\n\tskipIssueClosed   = \"issue_closed\"\n\tskipIssueBlocked  = \"issue_blocked\"\n\tskipWorkerRunning = \"worker_running\"\n)\n\n// excludedLabels are the labels that keep a PR out of a reviewer role's\n// queries: its own states and the guards.\nfunc excludedLabels(role string) []string {\n\treturn []string{\n\t\tlabels.Running(labels.StageReview, role), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, role), labels.Changes(role),\n\t\tlabels.ExecutorFailed, labels.NeedsHuman, labels.Hold, labels.TestsFailed,\n\t}\n}\n\n// candidates finds, per reviewer role, the PRs that request it and pass every\n// check. A review job of another role on the same PR does not exclude it:\n// reviewers run in parallel and their commits serialise on the branch lane.\nfunc (t *tick) candidates(ctx context.Context) ([]candidate, []error) {\n\tl := t.l\n\trunning, err := l.d.Store.RunningJobs(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, []error{fmt.Errorf(\"review: list running jobs: %w\", err)}\n\t}\n\tworkerBusy := map[int]bool{}\n\tfor _, j := range running {\n\t\tif j.Stage == \"worker\" {\n\t\t\tworkerBusy[j.Issue] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar out []candidate\n\tvar errs []error\n\tfor _, role := range t.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer) {\n\t\tq, err := query.RoleQuery{\n\t\t\tType: query.TypePR, Request: labels.Request(labels.StageReview, role.Name),\n\t\t\tStates: []string{labels.Running(labels.StageReview, role.Name), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, role.Name), labels.Changes(role.Name)},\n\t\t\tGuards: []string{labels.ExecutorFailed, labels.NeedsHuman, labels.Hold, labels.TestsFailed},\n\t\t}.Build()\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review role %s: %w\", role.Name, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\thits, err := l.d.Reader.SearchIssues(ctx, q, github.SearchOpts{Sort: \"created\", Order: \"asc\", Max: 50})\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf(\"review role %s: search: %w\", role.Name, err))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, hit := range hits {\n\t\t\tc, ok, err := t.consider(ctx, role, hit, workerBusy)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\terrs = append(errs, err)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif ok {\n\t\t\t\tout = append(out, c)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, errs\n}\n\nfunc (t *tick) skip(pr int, role, reason string) {\n\tt.log.Info(\"review.skip\", \"pr\", pr, \"role\", role, \"reason\", reason)\n}\n\n// consider re-reads PR hit.Number (search is eventually consistent) and its\n// issue, then applies the rules in the package comment.\nfunc (t *tick) consider(ctx context.Context, role config.Role, hit github.Issue, workerBusy map[int]bool) (candidate, bool, error) {\n\tl := t.l\n\tn := hit.Number\n\tpr, err := l.d.Reader.GetPR(ctx, n)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) {\n\t\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"review PR %d: re-read: %w\", n, err)\n\t}\n\tif pr.State != github.StateOpen || pr.Merged || !hasLabel(pr.Labels, labels.Request(labels.StageReview, role.Name)) ||\n\t\thasAny(pr.Labels, excludedLabels(role.Name)) {\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tif !strings.EqualFold(pr.Author, t.self) {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipNotAppPR)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tif pr.BaseRef != \"main\" {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipBaseNotMain)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\t_, issueN, ok := parseWorkerBranch(pr.HeadRef)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipNotWorkerRef)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tis, err := l.d.Reader.GetIssue(ctx, issueN)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) {\n\t\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueClosed)\n\t\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"review PR %d: read issue %d: %w\", n, issueN, err)\n\t}\n\tswitch {\n\tcase is.State != github.StateOpen || is.IsPR:\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueClosed)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\tcase hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.NeedsHuman) || hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.Hold):\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipIssueBlocked)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\tcase workerBusy[issueN]:\n\t\tt.skip(n, role.Name, skipWorkerRunning)\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, nil\n\t}\n\tok, err = t.recheck().Admitted(ctx, is)\n\tif err != nil || !ok {\n\t\treturn candidate{}, false, err\n\t}\n\treturn candidate{role: role, pr: pr, issue: is, since: hit.CreatedAt}, true, nil\n}\n\nfunc hasAny(have []string, want []string) bool {\n\tfor _, w := range want {\n\t\tif hasLabel(have, w) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc hasLabel(have []string, want string) bool {\n\tfor _, h := range have {\n\t\tif strings.EqualFold(h, want) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QAWgW7WGCERLp4eE1Lvf7E","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
